Hi [~accountid:610d3190ae72b2006f81ee2e],

Please below the external counsel advice on this matter as well as the draft response letter for Administration of Avenidas Novas.



{color:#36b37e}_Dear Beatriz,_{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}_According to Portuguese law, either party may terminate the lease agreement due to non-compliance by the other party, and "violation of rules of hygiene, silence, good neighbourly relations or rules contained in the condominium regulations" constitutes grounds for termination. In this case, the resolution by the landlord must be enacted by court decision, through an eviction action._{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}_Analysing the contract, we verified that its purpose is to exploit the bolt store. Thus, we prepared the answer, saying that the noise and the parking of the couriers is just what is necessary to achieve the purpose of the lease and there is nothing illegal about it._{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}_As for waste, we say that Bolt will work to ensure that situations such as those reported in the photographs do not happen again._{color}



{color:#36b37e}_With regard to waste, we would like to clarify that its collection is the responsibility of the Municipality of Lisbon, but that it is up to individuals to comply with the rules contained in the municipal regulations, especially with regard to the landfill of waste._{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}_Article 21. (Aviso n.º 20811-B/2019 that aproves «Regulamento de gestão de resíduos, limpeza e higiene urbana de Lisboa») says:_{color}

{color:#36b37e}_1 — It is only allowed to deposit urban waste in equipment made available for the effect, namely, according to the collection system implemented in the area, which should be used in such a way as to comply with adequate hygiene and health conditions._{color}

{color:#36b37e}_(…)_{color}

{color:#36b37e}_5 — Whenever the disposal equipment is at full capacity and it is not possible to use other nearby equipment, or due to a temporary lack of equipment disposal, due to loss, damage or any other reason, the user must retain the waste in his production local._{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}_Therefore, if Bolt does not have a place to deposit waste inside its store when the street bins are full, it should be considered asking to Municipality of Lisbon for more containers or managing the waste internally depending on the capacity of the bins installed._{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}_Available to clarify any additional doubts,_{color}

{color:#36b37e}_Kind regards_{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}_PS -  we just write the answer proposal (attached) in portuguese. If you need a translation, please let us know. On the other hand, if you prefer, I can also sign (as lawyer) and send the letter._{color}

[^resposta.docx]



Could you please confirm whether you would prefer the lawyer to sign the letter or whether you would prefer Manuel to sign it?

Should you have any further queries, please do let me know.

Many thanks!!

