It has a limitation on daily api call:
Standard Up to 10,000 Available to apps using any distribution channel
Raised Over 10,000 - limit subject to approval Must correctly implement API logic including retries
Available to apps using any distribution channel in addition to Google Play{{Nonce}} parameter is required in order to call the api: this field helps to protect against attack such as replay attacks, and person-in-the-middle (PITM) tampering attacks. It is better to generate this value on backend server and send to application to call integrity api:
{{nonce}} field must be correctly formatted: {{String}}

* URL-safe
* Encoded as Base64 and non-wrapping
* Minimum of 16 characters
* Maximum of 500 characters

There are two ways to use keys: Google-managed and self-managed encryption keys: It is recommended to use Google managed one:
Self-managed encryption keys should be stored on our own server: [https://developer.android.com/google/play/integrity/setup|https://developer.android.com/google/play/integrity/setup|smart-link] Integrity api help us to check below things: [https://developer.android.com/google/play/integrity/verdict|https://developer.android.com/google/play/integrity/verdict|smart-link] 
