{quote}If a new session is triggered (bc timeout, the user closes + reopens), I count this as distinct.{quote}

Probably this one is worth replacing with the user_id, as a car booking with a cancelation after will also alter a session id, which is rather a noise.
Sessions are important outside of the session duration threshold: if there were multiple trips per day, for example, a user id won't be as good.

But the difference there is really minor: a quote from the backend design

{quote}Overall there are 217406 user ids and 218110 sessions ids{quote}

