Hello\! 

To answer your questions: 

"{color:#333333}to what extent is this feature different from the Driver Prioritisation feature? If it is different, then why have we dropped Driver Prioritisation feature?"{color}

We haven't actually dropped {color:#333333}Driver Prioritisation feature, the previous results were reviewed and we're working on the next iteration.{color} 

"{color:#333333}to what extent is this feature different from the Driver Prioritisation feature"{color}{color:#333333}

Thank you for pointing this out, it is indeed similar, as in the mechanisms are almost the same. But the focus is different. In driver prioritisation feature, the focus is on providing more orders for drivers in higher priority level, which can be based on driver behaviour, but not only, to motivate the driver. 
The driver reordering feature focus is on providing the best suited driver to the order to improve the number of orders that are finished. The focus here is the rider. 

In future I expect these features to converge, as the inputs are similar, and we plan to have some UI components for this feature in future, but for this iteration they are treated as separate features.{color} 

 *{color:#333333} *Transparency angle -*{color} {color:#333333}we already have features like driver pricing and AV filter live in markes, which both remove some drivers from dispatching, based on either driver pricing or their historic behaviours, so if these are not taken into account, then we should.{color} 
 *{color:#333333} 
 *"Privacy angle*{color}{color:#333333}{color} {color:#333333}- we will be making automated decisions based on driver’s behaviour if this feature is applied. My understanding is that this is forbidden, unless it is needed for the performance{color} of driver’s{color:#333333} contract (T&Cs) with us. I am adding{color}{color:#333333}{color} [Liis Sokk|https://taxify.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=609f85c547ba02006fe1b9c3]{color:#333333}{color} {color:#333333}here for visibility. " - Can we have a call about this, I am not sure, how this can be forbidden. We are interested in providing the best solution for the riders on the app, if the driver behaviour is not satisfactory in terms of the service he'd provide, then it should be normal we depreoritise them? Or from another angle, we are prioritising drivers, who provide better service. This is not different from how other marketplaces like Amazon, youtube etc operate. + we are already scoring drivers for fraud, or block, based on acceptance scores, which also similarly is an automated decision.{color} 
